|------|--------|--------|
| env_set **value** refuse | TMPDIR `env_set(envc, "KEY", token)` | emit-c rc≠0 + `ERR\tsecret` + `env_set` |
| env_set **key** refuse | TMPDIR `env_set(envc, token, "public")` | emit-c `ERR\tsecret` |
| env_set clean (unused SECRET) | TMPDIR `env_set(envc, "KEY", "public")` | **no** `ERR\tsecret` (annotation rc=1 **OK**) |
| setenv value refuse | `fixtures/secret_setenv_fail.oo` | emit-c `ERR\tsecret` |
| setenv clean | `fixtures/secret_setenv_pass.oo` | **no** `ERR\tsecret` (do **not** `expect_ok` rc=0) |
| mmap path refuse | `fixtures/secret_mmap_fail.oo` | emit-c `ERR\tsecret` |
| mmap clean | `fixtures/secret_mmap_pass.oo` | **no** `ERR\tsecret` |
| unsetenv refuse | TMPDIR `unsetenv(envc, token)` | emit-c `ERR\tsecret` (sibling already in 2.3) |
| env_get dual-path control | `secret_env_get_{fail,pass}.oo` | fail refuse **emit+check**; pass rc=0 both |
| getenv leftover (honesty) | TMPDIR `getenv(envc, token)` | emit-c **no** `ERR\tsecret` today — **assert residual** (or flip if I3 lands) |
| check unlowered honesty | `check` on env_set fail | may be `ERR\ttype` undefined — **do not require** `ERR\tsecret`; **do not** treat type-fail as secret prove |
| Static 6.1 | grep three lists | `env_set` present; 2.3 family still listed |

**Helper:** `expect_secret_refuse` (emit-c) + `expect_no_secret` (grep −v `ERR\tsecret`; rc ignored).
